{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he commanded the first</b> — את four times, corresponding to the four kingdoms." "<b>ו</b> למי. Three times in the Masorah: this one and the others ולמי כל חמדת ישראל (and to whom — all the desire of Israel) and ולמי אני עמל (and to whom am I laboring). To say: all the desire of Israel and their labor — the sons of Esau took. And this is: ולמי כל חמדת ישראל / ולמי אני עמל / ולמי אלה לפניך. Another interpretation: Thus said Jacob: To whom am I laboring, to give all the desire of Israel — to whom are these before you?"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The three Masorah occurrences are Genesis 32:18 (ולמי אלה לפניך), Jeremiah 3:19 (ולמי אני עמל), and a third verse containing ולמי כל חמדת ישראל; the exact identity of the third citation is uncertain, possibly a paraphrastic conflation rather than a direct biblical quotation."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:36.691597193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}